# The Solesmes psalm tones with their usual endings, as in the Liber Usualis (1961).
# Transcribed from the tone table of jgabc by Benjamin Bloomfield, which is in the public
# domain (Unlicense): https://github.com/bbloomf/jgabc
#
# Each tone is a block: `name:`, `clef:`, `mediant:` and `termination:`, optionally `flex:`,
# separated by blank lines. A formula lists one GABC neume per syllable. The first `r` neume
# is the reciting note (the tenor): neumes before it are the intonation, and neumes after it
# up to the first accent are preparatory syllables. A neume after `'` falls on an accented
# syllable. A neume ending `r` takes any number of unaccented syllables, and the neumes after
# the last accent take the last syllables. A final `.` only ends the formula.

name: 1.D
clef: c4
mediant: f gh hr 'ixi hr 'g hr h.
termination: hr g f 'gh gr gvFED.

name: 1.D-
clef: c4
mediant: f gh hr 'ixi hr 'g hr h.
termination: hr g f 'g gr gvFED.

name: 1.D2
clef: c4
mediant: f gh hr 'ixi hr 'g hr h.
termination: hr g f gr 'gf d.

